{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1050,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We normally think of Telekinesis as a kind\nof supernatural mental power, but the word"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7050,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Telekinesis\" just comes from the greek kinēsis\nmeaning \"motion\" and tele- meaning \"at a distance\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12930,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the real universe is full of telekinesis,\nor motion at a distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16690,
    "dDurationMs": 3909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, what tells a ball to fall down when\nyou drop it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20599,
    "dDurationMs": 3131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why do magnets repel or attract without touching?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23730,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How does the sun heat us when it's millions\nof kilometers away?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27390,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And how do cell phones miraculously transport\nyour voice to the other side of town or the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32070,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other side of the earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33600,
    "dDurationMs": 5770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the sad truth about all of these real-world\nTelekinetic phenomena is that they aren't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39370,
    "dDurationMs": 2059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really action at a distance…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41429,
    "dDurationMs": 3581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as people figured out starting in the mid\n1800s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45010,
    "dDurationMs": 4919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before then, we didn't really know why magnets\ncould repel or attract each other from far"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49929,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away, how a ball could \"know\" that it was\nsupposed to fall towards the earth, or how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54989,
    "dDurationMs": 3561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sun could light up the earth - we just\nknew that they did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58550,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this was a kind of spooky action at a\ndistance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61890,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But into the world of physics came a London\nbookbinder's apprentice named Michael Faraday"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66890,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a young Scottish laird named James Clerk\nMaxwell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71050,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Together Magnetic Mike and J.C. made one of\nthe greatest discoveries of all time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76470,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Faraday was convinced by his experiments that\nmagnetic and electric forces were not telekinetic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81290,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "action at a distance, but were really the\nexpression of some underlying physical..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86530,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87810,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He called that “thing” a field, because\nit was away from the object - like students"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92950,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a field trip away from school."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95850,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Inspired by the cleverness of this idea, Maxwell\nsat down with pencil and paper and put together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101750,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the experimental results with Faraday's hunch\nusing beautiful mathematics: he showed that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107570,
    "dDurationMs": 6140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could describe all of electricity and\nmagnetism with the idea of a field: a single,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113710,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“Electro” - “Magnetic” field, which\npermeates all of space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118380,
    "dDurationMs": 5550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The basic idea of a field as envisioned by\nMaxwell is that at every point in space there's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123930,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a number which tells you something about that\npoint."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128110,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That number might be a simple number, like\nthe temperature at that point, or the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131920,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of cats at that point; or it might be a complicated\nnumber, like the direction and speed the wind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137110,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is blowing or the number of atoms of strawberry\ncheesecake that have moved past in the last"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140950,
    "dDurationMs": 1030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141980,
    "dDurationMs": 5750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Make a chart of those numbers for every point\nin the universe, and that's what a field is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147730,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So young J.C. realized that at every point\nin space, in addition to a number telling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152870,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you the flow of strawberry cheesecake there,\nthere are also numbers telling you the strength"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157090,
    "dDurationMs": 3110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and direction of the electromagnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160200,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The mathematical equations he used to describe\nthese numbers also relate how the strength"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165200,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the field at one point in space affects\nthe strength at nearby points, and those at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170760,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their nearby points, and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173400,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's this electromagnetic field (and the\nway it changes from point to point) that helps"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178330,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explain how things like magnets and static\nelectricity and your cell-phone calls can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183810,
    "dDurationMs": 5090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have long-range effects without actually being\ntelekinesis, or, action at a distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188900,
    "dDurationMs": 6460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, a magnet generates a disturbance\nin the field that looks like... a magnetic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195360,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196360,
    "dDurationMs": 4459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when you move the magnet, Maxwell realized\nthat the bits of the field close to the magnet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200819,
    "dDurationMs": 3531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will change because the magnet changed its\nposition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204350,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then the bits of the field a little farther\naway change because the field next to them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208900,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209900,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then the bits farther away, and even farther\naway, and so on like the tiniest bucket brigade"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214430,
    "dDurationMs": 5970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the universe, until they eventually push\non another magnet - maybe, a compass needle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220400,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, an electron makes a disturbance\nin the field that just says “hey, get away"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225380,
    "dDurationMs": 5350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from me!” to other electrons - but if you\nshake an electron around, it'll send out ripples"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230730,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the field like waves on a lake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233630,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The awesome thing that J.C. realized was that\nthese electromagnetic “ripples” or “waves”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239670,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "travel at the same speed as light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242390,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243390,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245200,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "J.C. had discovered that light is an electromagnetic\nwave!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249960,
    "dDurationMs": 4109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's these waves which are the bucket\nbrigade that transmits heat from the sun to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254069,
    "dDurationMs": 4611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the earth or a signal from your cell phone\nto your mother's or light from a lightbulb"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258680,
    "dDurationMs": 1289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to your eye."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259969,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only reason we think any of these things\nare “action at a distance” is that we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264199,
    "dDurationMs": 4351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can't see the hidden bucket brigade going\non under our very noses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268550,
    "dDurationMs": 4669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's there, as countless experiments since\nFaraday's have shown."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273219,
    "dDurationMs": 6361,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, Magnetic Mike and J.C. and their description\nof electromagnetic fields explained magnets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279580,
    "dDurationMs": 4839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and electricity and light without any need\nfor telekinesis or other kinds of action at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284419,
    "dDurationMs": 1161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285580,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the process, they laid the foundations\nfor all of 20th century physics - because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290960,
    "dDurationMs": 5799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "today, fields are the cornerstone of our understanding\nof the universe."
    } ]
  } ]
}
